            "creation_time": "2025-10-16T20:31:57Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3557\nChange methods-message to character(), not \"\"\n\n(hit submit by mistake on the original issue)\n\nA minor thing, but using `\"\"` instead of `character()` prevents us from doing nice code like\n\n```\n...\n\nreport <- .check_packages_used(...)\nif (!any(lengths(report)) {\n  return(...)\n}\n...\n```\n\nWe can see that in the patch -- in `format.check_packages_used`, all the other components use an `if (xx <- length(x$...))` check whereas we have `if (nzchar(x$methods_message))`. (in fact, we could simplify a bit further and drop the `if()` since `c(..., character())` will just drop the empty input, but I left it as is to keep the parallel structure).\n\nPS for purely internal, minor things like this, I'm still not sure the preferred way to report among (1) discuss first on r-devel [way too high barrier for an internal change IMO] (2) file on Bugzilla [might give the impression this is a \"bug\" when strictly speaking nothing's \"broken\"] (3) reach out to a single R-core member responsible for recent changes in this part of the code [I think it's best to avoid that except for highly-specific work in one member's core area of expertise]",
            "bug_id": 18958,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 1
          }
        ]
      }
